think Door one measured before it was touched. grain-pheromone owns no .gnupg-rye and no .ssh at all; its gpg.program named petrichor's wrapper and every IdentityFile named petrichor's keys. agent-jail.sh binds one tree, so from inside its own jail pheromone could neither sign nor connect -- and at a host prompt every check passed, because there the sibling is right there.
think The design was deliberate, not sloppy: birth_a_clone.rish's own comment reads host-shared custody material behind per-clone config, so every newborn signs as the one keeper. Sound thrift on a single-tree pier, unrunnable under a one-tree-per-jail enclosure. Two decisions each correct alone, and nothing owning the seam.
think Chose to copy the keys pheromone already named rather than generate fresh. Copying changes no trust relationship -- GitHub already accepts those keys -- and only reachability was broken. A fresh key would have blocked pheromone's push entirely until Keaton uploaded it. Repair the fault; do not smuggle a policy change into it. The fresh-key-per-ship option is named for him as a door.
think Door two is worse than reported. fleet_round_open.sh runs reset --hard on live trees every twenty minutes and modeled no interrupted rebase, so all three later steps misread one: the conflicted worktree reads dirty and gets stashed, HEAD is detached at a half-replayed commit and gets classified, and the reset abandons the rebase leaving the branch behind.
think Ran the new control against the elder script rather than trusting the reasoning. It printed already on the anointed order and open on 45c9c0fd26 -- a healthy open reported over a corpse -- and failed 5 of 14 legs. That is the fault demonstrated rather than argued.
obs Both faults sit where no standing guard could reach. .git/config and .git/ssh_config_jail are untracked by design because they carry custody paths, so tracked_link_scan, the commit hook, and the link duty are each blind to them by construction. The new scan reads untracked working-tree files, which is the one way the reading exists at all.
obs Ran the repaired round-open on this live tree to check for regression and it stashed my six uncommitted files -- correct behaviour, recovered with stash pop, and a reminder that a round-open is not a read-only check.
obs Folded %423-%426 to a shelf before booking; REDS stood at 1,034 bytes free and two rows would not fit. The four shared a theme worth naming: each was right about everything it looked at and wrong about the ground it never looked at.
obs Copied the-baton.md over its .mdc twin and dropped the twin's frontmatter; caught it by reading the elder from git rather than assuming the copy was clean.
loom key_locality trees=3 paths_checked=16 foreign=0 control_legs=13
loom round_open control_legs=14 elder_fails=5
